Description: Follow the Partners page when the person set up no instance
 KDE's text add-ons (KMail's AI Chat, Ask AI and quick answers, Kontact, the
 Sieve editor) keep their engines in one file, autogeneratetextinstances.
 When it holds none, they now take the edition's system default for text,
 and a program's own choice beside it, from System Settings, Partners
 (sparky-stereo-partners resolve --kind text --program DESKTOP-ID): an Ollama
 interface becomes one instance in memory, written to the file only when the
 person changes its settings, which makes it theirs. Other interfaces are
 left alone and said in the log: the llama.cpp add-on of 2.1.2 is not
 finished (its manager's requests are TODO) and the generic add-on knows no
 provider's own address. With sparky-stereo-partners installed, "Start
 Ollama" becomes "Open Partners": the engine is turned on there, as its user
 service on the card the person chose, not started by a program behind that
 switch. Without sparky-stereo-partners nothing changes.
Author: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-21
---
